  'Salt and black pepper to taste': 'Letswai le pepere ye ntsho go ya ka tatso',
  'Cover the soaked beans with fresh water, bring to a boil, then simmer uncovered for 45-55 minutes until a bean crushes easily between your fingers. Keep a cup of the cooking water.': 'Khupetša dinawa tše di inetšwego ka meetse a mafsa, di bedise, ke moka di bedise ka bonolo ntle le sekhurumelo metsotso ye 45-55 go fihlela nawa e pšhatlega gabonolo magareng ga menwana. Boloka komiki ya meetse a go apea.',
  'In a second pot, heat the oil over medium heat and cook the onion for 6-8 minutes until soft and golden.': 'Ka pitšeng ya bobedi, fiša makhura mollong wa magareng gomme o apee eiye metsotso ye 6-8 go fihlela e boleta e bile e le ya gauta.',
  'Stir in the garlic and curry powder and cook for 30 seconds, just until fragrant.': 'Hudua konofolo le phoofo ya kheri gomme o apee metsotswana ye 30, go fihlela go nkga gabotse.',
  'Add the grated tomato and simmer for 8 minutes until it darkens into a thick gravy.': 'Oketša tamati ye e gratilwego gomme o bedise ka bonolo metsotso ye 8 go fihlela e fifala e ba moro wo o tiilego.',
  'Fold in the drained beans with a splash of the reserved water. Simmer for 10 minutes so the beans take on the gravy, then season and serve over pap or rice.': 'Tsenya dinawa tše di tšholotšwego meetse le meetse a mannyane ao o a bolokilego. Bedisa ka bonolo metsotso ye 10 gore dinawa di hwetše moro, ke moka o tšhele dinoko o fe le bogobe goba reisi.',
